                    <h2 class="sub">                    Supercardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The N/D767a is a handheld dynamic vocal microphone incorporating E-V&#8217;s &#8220;VOB&#8221; (Vocally Optimized Bass) EQ circuit to reduce boominess from close-miked sources.</p><p>The supercardioid pickup pattern reduces bleed from nearby instruments.</p><blockquote><p><cite>Performing Musician, 2009</cite></p><p>The N/D767a &#8230; sounded very even and clear at modest volume. [At louder volumes], we were still pleased with the results and especially with its smooth character, particularly on the female vocals. On very loud passages the sound warmed up somewhat &#8230; but still cut through well.</p></blockquote><p><p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Electro-Voice/N-D767a">Electro-Voice N/D767a</a> is also known as: N/D767, ND767.</p>
